[1662.165958,"o","\u001b[0m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n  Observe the traffic interface\r\n  =============================\r\n\r\n  Attach accounting to the existing traffic0 interface and enable its\r\n  per-IP map. No new interface or replacement daemon is needed.\r\n\r\n  For a MikroTik operator, /tool/torch is a familiar source/port/protocol\r\n  attribution concept. Ze's show traffic usage reports cumulative IPv4\r\n  byte totals instead of Torch's transmit/receive rates.\r\n"]
